Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||01-24-2001||08:50 PM||||I am getting an 86 or possibly an 88 fiero for free from a person who let it sit for 5 years because he didnt want to buy a new timing gear for it, and he just wants to get rid of it. As far as I know it is a 4 banger, and it isnt the coupe. what things should I know about? where can a get good parts cheap? (Im just a poor college student who needed wheels)<P>Thank you||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||01-24-2001||08:55 PM||||If you get the 88 with a 4-banger, than it is a coupe.  GT, Formula, and Coupe were the only models in 88.  Let us know what you get though.  <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  is a good source for parts.  Theie prices are pretty decent but expect to pay more for 88 parts than pre 88 cars.  good luck and welcome to the forum!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||01-24-2001||09:02 PM||||If its a non-coupe 4 banger then it has to be an SE.  So its not an '88.  Ed Parks in Alabama has good used parts if you are looking for a cheap way out.  Also <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carparts.com</A>  is waaaay cheaper then the Fiero Store, but its a trade off because the Fiero Store has 10 times better customer service/shipping times.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||01-24-2001||09:07 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com</A>   has lots of used parts and is in Lebanon Ct.  not too far from Troy.||||reg||1
